 "description": "The Sidecar on an Analog Four MKII: knob D of the NOISE page picks a machine for a track's sound, and that track's trigs and parameters go to a Sidecar over USB MIDI under the A4 device profile. Its audio comes back through stock's Overbridge track inputs, into the voice's analog path. Every sound starts OFF. A track with a machine has OSC1's page as its own, and OSC2's by a setting, with plain dials and its names, and the Sidecar's pages can open on the A4's screen. Runs on a unit on Overbridge. Needs the A4 companion (mod sidecar), which carries the host link. From 0.14 the A4's half of the Sidecar sequencer's edit route (a4_seq.c): seq mode on a seq track in GRID REC, its trig keys, PAGE and encoders to the Sidecar, the Sidecar's trig and PAGE LEDs, copy / paste / clear reports, and no live recording on a seq track.",
 "device": "analog-four-mk2",
 "os": "1.56",
 "sources": ["a4_report.c", "a4_page.c", "a4_label.s", "a4_remote.c", "a4_seq.c"],
